  "domain_genes_absent_from_rna_sheet": 28,
  "reading": "On 5,011 C. elegans putative enhancers accessible in exactly one of five tissues (Serizay et al. 2020) with constraint measured on their exon-free bases (UCSC ce11 phyloP135way, cut re-derived at 5% FDR by Zoonomia's procedure), the domain-rule gene is expressed at 5 TPM or more and highest in the element's own tissue for 2,093 of 3,865 constrained elements (54.2%), against 51.5% for the 1,109 not constrained at the same tissue, position class, distance and measured length; difference +2.63 points, 95% -1.35 to +7.03 over 1-Mb clusters (within-stratum permutation p 0.105; FALSIFIED). No difference was detected: on this endpoint constraint adds no detectable tissue information to the domain rule's position. This is not evidence that constrained elements lack function. Conservation and accessibility are not function, and this run does not separate regulatory constraint from transcription-linked constraint.",
